# Do not repeat yourself

If the same or clearly similar code appears **3 or more times**, refactor into a shared helper, function, method, component, hook, or constant instead of copying again.

## Apply when

- Writing new code that would be a third copy of an existing pattern
- Editing a file and noticing a repeated block already at or above three uses
- Parallel branches that only differ by a value or type (parameterize)

## Prefer

- One named function/method with clear parameters
- Shared component or small utility in the nearest sensible package
- Constants / maps for repeated literals or switch-like duplication

## Avoid

- Premature abstraction for a one-off or second copy (two is usually fine until a third)
- Mega-utilities that hide unrelated concerns just to “dedupe”
- Copy-paste with tiny renames when a parameter would suffice

## Examples

```go
// ❌ third copy of the same pointer-string log formatting
debuglog.Printf("name=%v", name)
debuglog.Printf("real=%v", realName)
debuglog.Printf("race=%v", race)

// ✅ shared helper after the pattern repeats
debuglog.Printf("name=%s", debuglog.Str(name))
```

```tsx
// ❌ third near-identical status/button block
// ✅ extract a component or shared handler once you need it again
```
